#
# Counter-example for math:RandomVariableScopedShape (Rule P5): a math:RandomVariable that
# declares its math:randomVariableDomain and a math:hasDistribution context but OMITS its
# math:randomVariableCodomain, so that property's sh:minCount 1 fires —
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UnscopedRandomVariable).
# Single violation: the domain arm stays SATISFIED, and the node-level sh:or
# (hasDistribution OR a probability-space domain) is SATISFIED by the present
# math:hasDistribution; that distribution names its math:distributionFamily so
# math:DistributionFamilyShape (P6a) stays satisfied and supplies no parameters so
# math:DistributionParameterizationShape (P6b) / math:ParameterRoleCardinalityConstraint (P7)
# stay silent — EXACTLY ONE finding, no sibling shape also fires.
# Back-reference: math:RandomVariable / math:UnscopedRandomVariable (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecRandomVariableUnscopedBad).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:unscopedVariable a math:RandomVariable ;
    math:randomVariableDomain ex:sampleDomain ;
    math:hasDistribution ex:heightDistribution .

ex:sampleDomain a math:MeasurableSpace .

ex:heightDistribution a math:Distribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:normalFamily .

ex:normalFamily a math:DistributionFamily .
